zoe: Opening a short PR: migration checklist for autoscale schema v2 + Node/TS SDK snippet for setting scalePolicy and isolation. Need quick docs + API review. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1401

rick: Great, can you paste the Node snippet here? makes review faster.

zoe: Snippet: ```ts
import { RedwoodClient } from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new RedwoodClient();
await client.createReservedPool({
  name: 'dedicated-nyc',
  gpus: 4,
  labels: { pool: 'dedicated-nyc', team: 'search' },
  scalePolicy: { minReplicas: 1, maxReplicas: 12, cooldownSeconds: 90, burstCapacity: 3 },
  isolation: { type: 'reserved_pool', selector: 'pool=dedicated-nyc' }
});
```

priya: LGTM. Please add a JSON API example for folks calling the REST endpoint directly.

zoe: Added JSON example in the PR and pasted here: ```json
{
  "scalePolicy": {"minReplicas":1,"maxReplicas":12,"cooldownSeconds":90,"burstCapacity":3},
  "isolation": {"type":"reserved_pool","selector":"pool=dedicated-nyc"}
}
```

docs-bot: Linkcheck: detected broken link: `/sdk/node/old-client` -> suggested replacement `/sdk/node/client`. Automated patch created on branch.

luis: Small doc notes: call out that `grace_period_seconds` only applies to `soft` eviction and is ignored for `hard` eviction. Also clarify `burstCapacity` is expressed in GPU units.

zoe: Added both notes and a tiny troubleshooting checklist: "If reserved pool never scales: verify selector labels, confirm GPU quota, check cooldownSeconds and burstCapacity exhaustion."

terry: Tiny nit: prefer "service-level target" instead of "SLA" for user-facing docs.

zoe: Updated wording. Ran local linkcheck; docs-bot patch applied.

